foir, a CPU N64 RDP renderer (GPL-3.0-or-later, see LICENSE), from mupen64plus-pow2's ext/mupen64plus-rdp-foir
at pow2 commit a4585a2 (watch-src clone, 2026-11-24). Only the renderer is here: parser, setup, raster, TMEM,
kernels, spec, mt, stats, overdraw, vi, config, log. The m64p plugin, GL output, capture and frame log files are
left out. rename-foir.h (pow2's bundle/, generated by its gen-rename.py) prefixes every global name with foir_.

Joey64 uses it only for N64_RDP_CPUCOPY (off by default): a CPU copy of the RDP's drawing, kept in a private
shadow of RDRAM, so a smart-sync read fault can be answered without waiting for the GPU
(joey64-notes docs/foir-readback-study.md). Changes to these files are marked "Joey64:".
